OL,3,GNEWSAZoo future 'very positive' despite
OL,4,Apressures
OL,5,
OL,6,FJersey Zoo's future is "very positive"
OL,7,Fdespite the financial challenges facing
OL,8,Fthe conservation charity behind it,
OL,9,Faccording to its director of zoo
OL,10,Foperations.
OL,12,FThe optimistic message from Mark Habben
OL,13,Fcomes after zoo owner the Durrell
OL,14,FWildlife Conservation Trust reported a
OL,15,Fnet deficit of #3.9m in 2025, and
OL,16,Facknowledged pressure on its finances.
OL,18,FHabben, who joined Jersey Zoo in
OL,19,FJanuary after senior roles at London
OL,20,FZoo, Whipsnade Zoo and the Wildwood
OL,21,FTrust, said: "I think the future looks
OL,22,Fvery positive."
OL,23,APub: 19-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Ch Is NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
FL,444,440,260,160,0,100
